es_S U',\n(x_0, u', x_1) \\mapsto (x_0, x_1, u').\n$$", "MATH_0030": "$(x_0, u') \\in V \\Rightarrow (x_1, u') \\in V$", "MATH_0031": "$x_0, x_1, u'$", "MATH_0032": "$S$", "MATH_0033": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0034": "$V$", "MATH_0035": "$U \\subset U'$", "MATH_0036": "$X \\times_S U' \\to U'$", "MATH_0037": "$X \\to S$", "MATH_0038": "$X \\times_S U' \\to U'$", "MATH_0039": "$U \\subset U'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-characterize-quasi-affine}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-base-change-quasi-affine}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-descending-types-morphisms}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-characterize-quasi-affine}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{coherent-lemma-flat-base-change-cohomology}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{lemma-affine}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-descending-property-affine}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fpqc-quotient-topology}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0005": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:faba772bb2b7e8ab24022ad0c943213f9f84c1e5bc709eebcc2cfed7bc27e689", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d8ead474e35360edeb49fcf8824df1f76d899959cfe12e99d90e3dff95347f87", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nBeing quasi-affine is a property of morphisms of schemes\nwhich is preserved under any base change, see\nMorphisms, Lemmas <REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\nHence Lemma <REF_0003> applies\nand it suffices to prove the statement of the lemma\nin case the fpqc-covering is given by a single\n<MATH_0001> flat surjective morphism of affines.\nSay <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> so\nthat <MATH_0004> is a faithfully flat ring map.\nLet <MATH_0005> be a descent datum relative to <MATH_0006> over <MATH_0007>\nand assume that <MATH_0008> is quasi-affine.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nAccording to Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0004>\nthis means that\n<MATH_0009>\nis a quasi-compact open immersion of schemes over <MATH_0010>.\nThe projections <MATH_0011> are flat\nand hence we have\n<MATH_0012>\nby flat base change\n(Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <REF_0005>).\nThus the isomorphism <MATH_0013> (which\nis an isomorphism over <MATH_0014>) induces an isomorphism\nof quasi-coherent sheaves of algebras\n<MATH_0015>\non <MATH_0016>.\nThe cocycle condition for <MATH_0017> implies the cocycle condition\nfor <MATH_0018>. Another way to say this is that it produces\na descent datum <MATH_0019> on the affine scheme <MATH_0020> relative to\n<MATH_0021> over <MATH_0022>, which moreover has the property that the morphism\n<MATH_0023> is a morphism of descent data.\nHence by Lemma <REF_0006>\n(or by effectivity of descent for quasi-coherent\nalgebras) we obtain a scheme <MATH_0024> with an isomorphism\n<MATH_0025> of descent data.\nWe note in passing that <MATH_0026> is affine by\nLemma <REF_0007>.\n\n<STRUCT_0004><STRUCT_0005>\nAnd now we can think of <MATH_0027> as a (quasi-compact)\nopen <MATH_0028> with the property that\nit is stable under the descent datum\n<MATH_0029>\nIn other words <MATH_0030>\nfor any <MATH_0031> mapping to the same point of <MATH_0032>.\nBecause <MATH_0033> is surjective we immediately find that\n<MATH_0034> is the inverse image of a subset <MATH_0035> under\nthe morphism <MATH_0036>.\nBecause <MATH_0037> is quasi-compact, flat and surjective\nalso <MATH_0038> is quasi-compact flat and surjective.\nHence by Morphisms, Lemma <REF_0008>\nthis subset <MATH_0039> is open and we win.\n<STRUCT_0006>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7b423d89312703744bcd69dce2cc758620cc16900fba627a2f2ad9990af40e07", "unit_id": "inventory:descent:0247:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "neighbor:inventory:descent:02W4:paragraph/0001", "hash": "sha256:b1a6fa5536201fbae408a1be7bc09dc8a61add50f9c9eee9220b157b5902e760", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"